Romhack Base: Minish Cap
Timeline Placement: Not too long after Minish Cap
Length: Long (2 full Romhacks)
Significance: Emotional journey for Link; Significant lore implications

Synopsis:
[Installment 1: The Simulation Incident]
It is dismal and raining. Link is awake in bed. He gets up without the usual bounce. The house is quiet except the rain. Elzo's last gift to him sits in a dusty corner with other things.
Link heads downstairs. Entering Master Smith's room, he might imagine seeing his grandfather for a moment, but illusion is immediately replaced with reality: Smith is gone.
Link leaves the house. It is still raining. (Link's voice may be a bit deeper, and doesn't vocalize as often.)
Houses are locked, or else people have nothing interesting to say.
The King, like Smith, has also passed away. Zelda is busy with new queenly duties. No time for Link. (There hasn't been any music as of yet.)
Minish portals don't work. There's no monsters. No collectibles. No one wants to fuse kinstones.
The path to the Royal Valley is open, but Link refuses to head that way.
Link enters Simon's Simulations.
Simon seems to have been expecing him. (If Simon is worried about Link using his services excessively, he keeps it hidden under good business sense.)
Link enters the dream. He fights monsters. When they're all gone, he opens the chest.
Lightning strikes the building. It shocks the bed with Link in it. Simon gets startled.
The lights in the simulation flicker. The chest turns into the great Bound Chest. It pops open, releasing creepy mask monsters. They circle Link, then attack as one.
Link blacks out.
When he comes to, all his items have been stolen. A large dark crack has been made in the north wall.
A hologram of Simon appears, asking Link if he's okay. Simon gets to debugging. Link enters the crack.
Simon says to wait, but his message loses signal and is cut off. Link has no choice but to continue.
Link completes a mini-dungeon that is like a circuitboard, complete with new electronics-inspired puzzle devices.
The first boss is one of the mask monsters: it uses Link's stolen small shield. Use the environment to defeat it and get the shield back. (Each major item is reobtained from a mask monster using it.)
Making it out of the first area, Link enters a dark digital version of the Elemental Sanctuary. There are 4 doors, one in each corner of the room. There is a Dark Sword in the pedestal.
Simon's hologram appears. He orders Link to take the Dark Sword.
Link may obey. He may refuse.
The four doors lead to four regions: Minish Woods, Mt Crenel, Lake Hylia, and Wind Ruins. (Things proceed much like the Short Version.)
There are no hearts or fairies anywhere, but occasionally there is a room with a random NPC who heals Link.
Simon's hologram tells Link to do a spin attack with the Dark Sword to destroy and absorb each Safe Room and its illusionary NPC, upgrading the blade. Link may obey or refuse.
- Link starts with all Tiger Scrolls, the Kinstone Bag, the Jabber Nut, the Power Bracelets, and the Graveyard Key.
- The north door in the town well leads to Castor Wilds, where the Bow is obtained in the usual minish hole.
- The eyegore in Fortress of Winds blocks not the boss door, but the entrance to the Cloud Tops, where Roc's Cape can be obtained after gathering and using the Cloud Top Gold Kinstones.
- To the west of Minish Woods, there are the Eastern Hills, where use of the bow and roc's cape helps Link obtain 1 of 3 Castor Wild Kinstones.
- To the west of Lake Hylia, there is Lon Lon Ranch, where the same enable him to get the 2nd Castor Wild Kinstone.
- In Melari's Mines is the 3rd Castor Wilds Kinstone, also blocked with need of the bow and roc's cape.
- The 3 Castor Wilds Kinstones opens the way to the southwest in Castor Wilds, which leads to the Castor WIlds Darknut and the Veil Falls Gold Kinstone.
- A path near Lake Hylia leads to the Veil Falls dig caves (connected), which open onto Veil Falls. Use the Gold Kinstone as usual. At the top, there is a cave/hole instead of a tornado.
- In the cave at the top of Veil Falls is a dungeon combining the trials for the flippers and the power bracelets, though the item here is the Grip Ring.
- Climb the wall to the Cave of Flames to find the Cane of Pacci. (No major boss can be fought yet.)
- Use the Cane of Pacci to enter the Temple of Droplets on the far eastern end of Lake Hylia. Inside is the Flame Lantern.
- The Flame Lantern is useful in Deepwood Shrine, reached through the minish path behind the Mayor's Cabin. The Gust Jar is within.
- Entering the Palace of Winds, the item within is the Magical Boomerang.
- Somehow Link gets to the Graveyard, where the Graveyard Key he's had from the start comes in handy. After completing the area, he meets enters the Royal Crypt and finds himself in the throne room.
If Link has used the Dark Sword, he is met with Simon's Hologram, and Ending 1 commences. If he refused, he is met with Smith and King Daltus, who grant him the Four Sword, commencing Ending 2.
Ending 1:
- Simon's Hologram uses the Dark Sword to perform a Dark Rite on Link.
- Link wakes up in Simon's Simulations. The real Simon is crying/sweating profusely. Princess Zelda wakens from Link's bedside, glad to see him awake at last.
- Link acts strange. His eyes are shadowed. He gets up without a word and leaves.
- The worried Zelda becomes the player character. She follows after Link, who is heading north.
- Zelda picks up the Bow of Light, discarded into a river by the road.
- Zelda gets trapped in North Hyrule Field with 2 moblins, the same way Vaati trapped Link in the original adventure.
- Entering the Castle Courtyard, she finds that Link has attacked the guards.
- Catching up with him, she finds him beating on the castle doors. He stops, turns, brandishes the Dark Sword and laughs Vaati's laugh.
- Link and Zelda fight.
- Defeating Link causes him to fall to sleep, and Zelda can't wake him.
Ending 2:
- With the Four Sword the Bosses can now be defeated.
- Upon reentering the Elemental Sanctuary after defeating all bosses, Simon's Hologram gets angry, and the Dark Sword animates into Dark Link. Defeating Dark Link opens the north door.
- A second part to the initial circuitboard dungeon commences. The Boss is Mazaal.
- At the end, Simon's Hologram itself challenges you in the dark version of the Castle Courtyard. He summons many enemies in Phase 1, and fights like Agahnim in Phase 2. (Consider Puppet Ganon music.)
- The door to the Elemental Sanctuary leads instead to the inside of an armos. Flip the switch to reboot the Simulation.
- Return quickly to the original Simulation Room as the place collapses around you.
- In the original room, defeat the animated version of the three-eyed purple slime monster mascot as seen on the top of Simon's building.
- Win, and awaken, with Zelda joyful beside you and Simon swearing to only sell pickles instead.
- After the credits, Link sleeps peacefully in bed at home... when a shadow appears behind his bed and grins.

[Installment 2: The True Nightmare World]
<Part 1>
Continues from either ending of Installment 1. Link is still asleep. Zelda is worried.
Simon has thrown out the offending bed. It now gets moldy deep within the Royal Valley forest. Zelda may need to do some things first to enter the dream there.
The dream world appears as a darkened and broken-up version of the simulated world from Installment 1, spanning singularly from the original room to the armos power switch.
In the armos power switch room, there is a huge hole in the ground showing the cosmic sky only seen in Vaati's 3rd arena.
Zelda jumps down into that sky.
<Part 2>
Awakening on a crumbling shore, an island above a vast purple sky (perhaps like cosmic sky, perhaps like the sky outside Dark Hyrule Castle), Zelda makes her way east.
The shore over the abyss continues along the south edge. The north is still barricaded, though she soon can see a frozen lake that way.
Zelda finds a house. There she meets the unassuming soldier/adventurer: Nakura. He agrees to aid her in searching for Link.
Things happen, I'm not sure what. Nakura might talk to piles of bones as though they were living people.
Nakura learns something unpleasant (perhaps that everyone else on the island is already technically dead). He doesn't take it too well, and flees.
Zelda goes thru a water cave dungeon for some reason. Upon emerging, she's ambushed by a moblin named Karuna. Nakura reappears to save her, but gets himself killed.
...
The thing is,
the whole Nightmare World
is a dark version of Koholint Island.
Zelda began on the far left corner of Toronbo Shores. The water cave dungeon was the Angler's Tunnel (and Zelda probably traverses Tail Cave, Bottle Grotto, and Key Cavern as well).
The frozen lake is Martha's Bay, covered with rail-tracks, and the Pothole Field is full of frosty graves.
Mabe Village is a ghost town, perhaps literally. The Animal Village is full of bones. Fiery tornados scour the fields, which are littered with old weapons.
The sands of Yarna Desert drain into the abyss. The Rapids Ride is bits of rock floating over the void (use the little whirlwinds here to traverse).
Lava pours from the western end of Tal Tal Mountain Range. The eastern end flows with poison.
The Mysterious Forest traps lost souls within. Goponga Swamp is just like Castor Wilds.
Kanalet Castle is a dark fortress. The Cemetary extends northward to the foot of Mt Tamaranch, where the bones of a great whale lay stark, and is thus renamed: Whalefall Mountain.
Anyway...
At the end of Zelda's adventure here, she finds Link asleep in the Dream Shrine. She falls asleep in a bed next to his, and fights Vaati (and perhaps Null) in his nightmare.
Link awakens, only in time to see Zelda snatched away from him.
<Part 3>
He tracks the enemy to Kanalet Castle, where he finds a gathering of shadowy villains. Just before he gets struck by them, someone shrinks him to minish size, and leads him to safety.
...
The thing is, the Nightmare World is also the Minish Homeworld. (Minish may technically be the incarnations of children who died too young to experience life.)
And Link is saved by Ezlo himself.
Turns out that the reason the minish are so tiny and can only be seen by the pure of heart, is that they cast a spell on themselves to protect themselves from the evils of their world.
Anyway, tearful reunion aside (and a funny little scene where old Ezlo can't keep up with Link and must turn into a hat), Link and Ezlo set out to beat the villains and save Zelda.
(If Zelda wasn't here, Ezlo would have sent Link back home in a heartbeat, for the monsters here are daunting.) (Also Link can shrink again!) (A minish may want mysterious shells in the Seashell Mansion...)
So:
- Northeast Corner, in Eagle's Tower, is Veran. She possesses the Siren: Martha the Mermaid. <Phase 1: Possessed Mermaid. Phase 2: Dark Fairy.>
- Northwest Corner, in Turtle Rock, is Onox. He guards the Siren: Madam MeowMeow. <Phase 1: Iron Knuckle. Phase 2: Dark Dragon.>
- In Martha's Bay/Catfish's Maw is Malladus. He possesses the Siren: Crazy Tracy. <Phase 1: Possessed Maiden. Phase 2: Fiery Skull.>
- In Kanalet Castle is Simon's Hologram/Fake Ezlo Wizard/Fake Ezlo Giant Cap/Facade/Chancellor Cole. He has to be dealt with at some point.
- In the Ancient Ruins/Face Shrine is Twinrova, guarding the Siren: Marin. <Phase 1: Twin Sisters. Phase 2: Combined Form.>
Gather all 4 Sirens at Mt Tamaranch to play the Majora's Mask version of the Ballad of the Windfish, hoping to resurrect the dead whale and restore the world to better times.
- Martha plays the Conch Horn.
- Madam MeowMeow plays the Full Moon Cello.
- Crazy Tracy plays the Thunder Drum.
- Marin plays the Surf Harp.
Within the Wind Fish's Bones is the final boss: DethI/Gomess/Null. Defeat it to change the shape of the Nightmare World into the Dream World of Koholint, and return Link and Zelda to Hyrule.


[Leftover Ideas]
Happy Hearth Inn: Sleep in each of the 3 beds to access 3 dreams, each of increasing difficulty, and obtain 3 keys needed to access the next location in the plot.
Nayru's Music Hall: Herb has turned his phonograph house into a proper music hall, where Nayru sings on stage.
- Sheet Music is hidden in chests throughout the world: find a chest to get a song from the area.
- Bring Sheet Music to Nayru to add it to her repertoire: you can request her to sing it anytime (for a small fee?) in her own special style.
- Give her all Sheet Music in the world for a special reward.
Din's Dance Club: Din has taken over the Goron Cave with her popular new dance minigame. (Gorons resemble K-Pop fans in costume & dialogue.)
- Dance moves are based on different item-use animations?
Farore's House: Aided by Link and Zelda, Farore has moved into one of the trees that had a heart piece inside. (There is now a smokestack and door... Maybe not the tree in South Hyrule Field for propriety.)
- Her room has bookshelves and a desk wide enough for 3 books. Retrieve 3 special books for her, and when she reads them, you might fall asleep and experience special mini-dungeons.
Quest to retrieve all lost figurines? (Most expendable idea)
